# Services, selectors, tasks

- A service exists only for work spanning several models or an external system.
  One-model state changes stay model methods.
- Keyword-only arguments, explicit return types.
- `transaction.atomic()` around writes that must succeed together.
- Side effects (email, tasks, webhooks, cache busts) go in
  `transaction.on_commit` so a rollback cannot fire them.
- Celery tasks receive **ids**, never model instances, and must be idempotent.
- Raise a domain exception the caller can translate; log with context and
  re-raise anything unexpected.

See skills: `django-services`, `celery-patterns`, `django-logging`.
